     "answer": "### Report\n\n**Change IDs Applied:**\n- chg-d7aab7cf3171\n- chg-aa93cb7b8ac7\n- chg-038e4a2b1844\n\n**Expected kWh Saved:**\n- 11.65 kWh\n\n**Cells Left Awake and Why:**\n- **Coverage Cells (Layer Low):** These cells were left awake to ensure continuous service and to carry the moved traffic from the capacity cells that were put to sleep.\n  - s1-1/low\n  - s1-2/low\n  - s1-3/low\n  - s10-1/low\n  - s10-2/low\n  - s10-3/low\n  - s2-1/low\n  - s2-2/low\n  - s2-3/low\n\n- **Capacity Cells (Layers Mid and NR3500):** These cells were put to sleep to save energy, but some were kept awake due to higher traffic loads or specific operational requirements.\n  - s1-2/mid (partially awake due to higher traffic)\n  - s10-2/mid (partially awake due to higher traffic)\n  - s10-3/mid (partially awake due to higher traffic)\n  - s2-1/mid (partially awake due to higher traffic)\n  - s2-2/mid (partially awake due to higher traffic)\n  - s2-3/mid (partially awake due to higher traffic)\n\nThe changes were applied successfully, and the expected energy savings are 11.65 kWh. The coverage cells (layer low) were kept awake to ensure continuous service, while the capacity cells (layers mid and NR3500) were put to sleep to save energy. Some capacity cells were partially awake due to higher traffic loads or specific operational requirements.",
